WEBVTT

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.190
Hey, Shigeno!

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:05.610
I've got news!

00:00:05.610 --> 00:00:07.300
What's wrong?

00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:08.470
Why are you in a rush?

00:00:08.470 --> 00:00:10.320
"What's wrong?"

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.110
Gibson is coming out of retirement and is back on the Bisons!

00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.990
Wh-What?

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.830
egaita yume to koko ni aru ima

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.830
I look at my dream and my current reality,

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:30.130
futatsu no keshiki mikurabete mo

00:00:24.830 --> 00:00:30.130
but no matter how much I compare the two,

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:35.510
katachi wo kaete koko ni aru no wa

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:35.510
the only thing I truly have

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.810
tashika na hitotsuno mono

00:00:35.510 --> 00:00:40.810
is the one and only thing I'm sure of.

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:46.150
sugiyuku haru wo oshiminagara mo

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:46.150
Even as I bid a sad farewell to spring,

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:51.400
bokura no maku aketa ano natsu

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:51.400
the season of the coming summer began.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.780
ironna koto wo wakari hajimeta

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:56.780
I had begun to understand many things

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.870
aki to nanika ushinatta fuyu

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:02.870
by the fall, but I lost something in the winter.

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:08.420
garakuta no yama kara

00:01:02.870 --> 00:01:08.420
In the junk I've piled up,

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.510
sagasu ano hi no yume

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.510
I search for the dream I had way back when.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:17.800
hibike kono koe yo

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:17.800
Let my voice echo on.

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:24.060
hibike kono kokoro yo

00:01:17.800 --> 00:01:24.100
Let my heart resonate.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:29.730
namida kareru made

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:29.730
Until my tears dry up,

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:34.780
mada denu kotae oitsuzukete

00:01:29.730 --> 00:01:34.780
I'll chase the answer I've been searching for.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:40.120
namida hareru made

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:40.120
Until my tears clear away,

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:45.120
waga yukue mayoi nagara mo

00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:45.120
though I may lose my way,

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.960
egakikake no ima

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:48.960
I'll continue to paint the present,

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.460
kizamu

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:56.220
and carve my existence with my own two hands.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.750
akashi

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:56.220
kono te de

00:02:05.930 --> 00:02:09.960
Mr. Gibson, you collapsed in the World Cup,

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:12.230
and we were told you had retired.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:16.180
I don't recall saying anything about retiring.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:18.740
Now that I've recovered, I have enough confidence to keep playing.

00:02:18.740 --> 00:02:24.940
B-But isn't it a bit dangerous for you to return to pitching, given your heart problems?

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:26.810
That's not a problem.

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:28.410
I've got my doctor's approval.

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:31.470
B-But, Mister...

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:35.840
In the World Cup, you played alongside your son, Junior,

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:40.130
and were deemed the best in the world upon defeating Team Japan.

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:46.970
It was our understanding that you've had your glory moments and are now burned out as a major league player.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:50.670
Is there anything else you really need to do?

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.440
Ridiculous.

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:58.830
That's just nonsense fabricated by the ridiculous mass media.

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:03.620
I haven't been playing baseball in order to achieve something.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:09.080
Telling me that I burned out upon reaching the top is the greatest insult I could possibly receive.

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:12.840
In any case,

00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.710
I'll be pitching again starting with tomorrow's game.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.430
As much as I desire.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:21.760
W-Wait, Mister!

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.550
Please come back!

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.360
We still have questions.

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:25.970
Mister!

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:25.970
Please come back!

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.940
An Electrifying Return

00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:30.940
An Electrifying Return

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:49.240
You're doing pretty well these days.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.470
Got out of your slump, huh?

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:52.040
Yeah.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:55.790
I can finally see the pitches again.

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:58.550
I was worried about being sent back to the minors.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:00.890
Now you just need some home runs.

00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:05.080
Hits are good, but I'd really love to see those old home runs again.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.410
Next, today's sports headline.

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.520
We've received incredible news from the major league.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:18.440
We were told that Mr. Joe Gibson had retired upon finishing the World Cup in the spring,

00:04:18.900 --> 00:04:22.190
but he has made the shocking announcement that he'll be playing for the Chicago Bisons.

00:04:22.870 --> 00:04:24.990
Wh-What?!

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:30.970
We were certain of Mr. Gibson's retirement, as he is already forty-three years old,

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.710
but he denied it at the press conference.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.300
He has already been registered in the major leagues

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:38.670
and is preparing for tomorrow's Hornets game.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:38.670
Wow.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:41.080
Joe, your dad's still playing?

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:42.350
That's awesome.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:45.110
Looks like a father-son match might really happen.

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.760
I don't care about that!

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:49.150
I don't understand.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:51.750
What is that old man thinking?

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:52.950
He's so stupid.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.230
I'm home.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:04:58.830
Welcome home.

00:04:58.830 --> 00:05:00.150
Oh, Papa!

00:05:00.150 --> 00:05:01.780
Welcome home!

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:03.810
I love you.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.990
Chiharu, were you a good girl?

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:06.970
Yeah!

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:08.400
How was the trip?

00:05:07.710 --> 00:05:09.020
Pick me up!

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:09.780
Is Goro doing well?

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:12.280
Yeah, he is.

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:13.440
That's good.

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:17.120
Speak of the devil, maybe?

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:19.330
No, it's the television studio.

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.000
Chiharu, Papa has business to tend to.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:24.300
Business?

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:25.030
Yes.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:26.920
Yeah.

00:05:26.920 --> 00:05:28.590
I just got home.

00:05:30.950 --> 00:05:32.400
Is that true?

00:05:32.930 --> 00:05:34.260
No.

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:36.450
I didn't hear about that at all in America.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:39.280
Yes.

00:05:39.280 --> 00:05:40.170
I'll see you later then.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:42.970
Did something happen?

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.830
Gibson came out of retirement,

00:05:48.910 --> 00:05:52.490
and he'll be playing against the Hornets tomorrow.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.790
Isn't tomorrow...

00:05:55.170 --> 00:05:56.460
Yeah.

00:05:57.320 --> 00:05:59.670
Goro's starting tomorrow.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:05.050
Man, I almost pissed myself when I heard the news.

00:06:05.410 --> 00:06:09.670
Plus he's starting against us today.

00:06:09.670 --> 00:06:13.210
Honestly, I'm pretty happy I'll get to play him.

00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:16.910
I've been admiring Gibson since I was a kid.

00:06:16.910 --> 00:06:18.970
Yeah, same here.

00:06:19.650 --> 00:06:21.370
Hey, Shigeno.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:23.770
The news about Gibson is taking up the whole front page.

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:25.420
Want to read it?

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:26.690
No.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:30.510
I don't have a designated hitter today, so I need to get in some batting practice.

00:06:30.510 --> 00:06:32.030
And I can't read English.

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:40.460
You're pretty good, Shigeno.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:42.430
You've got a good swing.

00:06:43.850 --> 00:06:48.630
Telling me that I burned out upon reaching the top is the greatest insult I could possibly receive.

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:51.610
I don't get it.

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.850
I thought that old man had done enough by now.

00:06:57.800 --> 00:07:02.450
Even if the doctor gives the okay, he's got a heart problem.

00:07:02.450 --> 00:07:06.360
Why is he taking the risk and pushing himself?

00:07:06.890 --> 00:07:12.870
I thought he got what he wanted when he played in the World Cup and won.

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:17.700
Shigeno's pretty good.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:21.700
I got a call from Mr. Gibson.

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:25.210
He was pretty worried about how you've changed.

00:07:26.340 --> 00:07:28.130
Could Gibson...

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:35.450
We could even use Shigeno as a pinch hitter.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:42.240
G-Gibson!

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:47.650
Hey, Gibson!

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:49.820
H-Hey, please wait a second!

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:54.000
Yo.

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.190
It's been a while, Mister.

00:07:56.190 --> 00:08:00.160
You don't have to ignore me just 'cause we'll be pitching against each other today.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:03.220
I was honestly quite surprised.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:06.040
You're a persistent pitcher, I'll give you that.

00:08:06.430 --> 00:08:10.180
But it's also important in life to know when to call it quits.

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:15.950
You're in your early forties already, so shouldn't you take Junior's feelings into account?

00:08:17.210 --> 00:08:18.690
That's none of your business.

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:23.690
Wait up.

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:27.770
You're acting pretty hostile, but I know what this is.

00:08:27.770 --> 00:08:33.720
You just couldn't stand to watch Junior and I be so pathetic.

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:40.700
You came back to show us how it's done and get us fired up.

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:43.640
Well, get off the mound.

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:47.510
Junior and I don't want that.

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:52.380
You think I came back for you two?

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:54.410
Ridiculous.

00:08:54.410 --> 00:08:57.430
Don't flatter yourself.

00:08:57.900 --> 00:09:02.170
It's true that I'm disappointed in you and Junior,

00:09:02.170 --> 00:09:05.520
but who would come out of retirement for pathetic little brats like you?

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:10.320
You both just don't understand anything.

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:14.860
I don't feel good about pitching against you for my first game back.

00:09:14.860 --> 00:09:17.950
Don't even talk to me anymore, you weakling.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:23.430
Catcher,

00:09:23.430 --> 00:09:27.230
number 18: Rob Donnelly!

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:30.320
Starting pitcher,

00:09:30.320 --> 00:09:37.180
number 13: Joe Gibson!

00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:39.050
He's back.

00:09:39.050 --> 00:09:40.610
Bullet Joe!

00:09:40.610 --> 00:09:42.220
He's been in the league for twenty-one years!

00:09:42.720 --> 00:09:46.850
He's played for Texas, Tokyo, San Francisco, and New York.

00:09:46.850 --> 00:09:50.150
This great man is playing for Chicago this year!

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:52.600
This is his first game back.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:53.810
I wonder... if he's actually healthy.

00:09:52.600 --> 00:09:55.460
What sort of pitching will he show us today?

00:09:56.340 --> 00:09:59.530
Then, can I ask one thing of you?

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:06.000
Please keep being an amazing baseball player until Goro grows up.

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:10.580
He's already done more than enough for that promise.

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.430
You both just don't understand anything.

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:22.890
Stupid old man.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:27.020
I'm over here, worrying about your health, and that's how you act?

00:10:29.690 --> 00:10:32.110
Play ball!

00:10:47.240 --> 00:10:48.370
Strike!

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:52.650
89 mph?

00:10:52.650 --> 00:10:54.800
Was that a curve?

00:10:57.010 --> 00:10:58.450
Ball.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:00.710
Is that really Gibson's pitch?

00:11:00.710 --> 00:11:02.340
It looks kinda slow.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:03.010
Yeah.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:07.560
He's probably been taking his training easy during his recovery.

00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:20.200
The six straight strike outs I saw in the All-Star Game when I was a kid were amazing.

00:11:21.220 --> 00:11:23.940
I kept trying to mimic his pitching form.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.370
Ever since I was a kid,

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:30.510
he's been playing in the major leagues.

00:11:31.290 --> 00:11:36.390
I was hoping I'd have an opportunity to hit his pitches while he was still young!

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:40.450
It's through!

00:11:40.450 --> 00:11:42.220
Roy sprints to second base!

00:11:42.220 --> 00:11:44.280
A great chance for the Hornets.

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:45.690
A double right off the bat.

00:11:45.690 --> 00:11:48.980
Gibson's control and speed aren't as sharp as they used to be.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:52.730
Ball.

00:11:53.600 --> 00:11:54.150
Ball.

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.480
Ball two!

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:56.920
All right, good!

00:11:56.920 --> 00:11:58.150
Keep your eye on the ball.

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:02.990
His pitches are weak, and his control is bad.

00:12:03.370 --> 00:12:06.620
It was way too early for him to come back.

00:12:06.620 --> 00:12:07.160
Ball.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:08.840
What are you talking about?!

00:12:08.840 --> 00:12:10.960
He's just getting started!

00:12:10.960 --> 00:12:15.920
Even if he's out of shape, he's got the technique and the spirit to do this.

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:19.100
Hey, you're starting today, aren't you?

00:12:19.100 --> 00:12:21.590
Don't you want your team to win?

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.200
Ball! Ball four!

00:12:26.740 --> 00:12:31.420
Now hitting, number 1: Jeff Keene!

00:12:49.730 --> 00:12:50.990
It's good!

00:12:50.990 --> 00:12:55.590
Keene gets a three-run home run off that hit past right field!

00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:59.630
Gibson takes a home run in the first inning of his comeback game!

00:13:00.010 --> 00:13:02.920
That slider didn't bend very well.

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:07.340
Keene wouldn't miss an easy pitch like that.

00:13:08.470 --> 00:13:10.160
What the hell?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:13.730
You were being so obnoxious earlier, so what's going on, old man?

00:13:14.470 --> 00:13:15.480
Why?

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:18.610
Why did he come back?

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:23.390
Considering his age and stamina, he can't possibly do much more.

00:13:23.840 --> 00:13:26.080
Not to mention he has a bad heart.

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.070
I think I kind of understand.

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:37.250
There's still something he has to do as a professional.

00:13:37.250 --> 00:13:39.270
That's how Gibson feels.

00:13:39.270 --> 00:13:43.630
Now hitting, number 11: Parker!

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:47.390
You've grown old, Gibson.

00:13:47.390 --> 00:13:49.550
Your era...

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:51.850
has already ended!

00:13:58.660 --> 00:14:00.480
Another double?

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:02.110
What are you doing, Gibson?

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:04.460
This isn't good.

00:14:04.460 --> 00:14:06.220
Call the bullpen.

00:14:06.220 --> 00:14:06.900
Okay.

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:09.500
Ball.

00:14:10.500 --> 00:14:13.230
If he's just having a bad day, it's nothing to worry about,

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:14.660
but I wonder.

00:14:15.800 --> 00:14:19.420
He's just recovered, and he was out for two months,

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:23.780
but his age has been showing pretty clearly for a few years now.

00:14:25.080 --> 00:14:25.840
Ball.

00:14:26.680 --> 00:14:31.140
In the World Cup, he had the spirit to go as far as hiding his illness to play, but...

00:14:31.720 --> 00:14:37.860
Maybe he was able to hold down Japan with his skill because they weren't used to his pitches.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:43.770
He's switched to pitching breaking balls in recent years, but...

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:44.360
Ball!

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:49.910
For Gibson, he needs his powerful fastballs to scare off the batters.

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:53.070
Ball. Ball four!

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.220
Hey, is this a joke?

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:58.460
You haven't even gotten one out yet!

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:10.630
Now hitting, number 28: Dunstan!

00:15:16.320 --> 00:15:17.330
Out!

00:15:19.180 --> 00:15:21.140
Hey, Shigeno.

00:15:21.630 --> 00:15:24.170
If this keeps going, you might have to bat soon.

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:28.740
We should play it safe and take on the eighth and ninth batters with the bases loaded.

00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:32.010
No?

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:33.600
Then we only have one other choice.

00:15:33.600 --> 00:15:35.130
We'll pull you out of the game.

00:15:35.130 --> 00:15:38.320
We can't give up any more runs today.

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.670
No.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.170
I understand.

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:48.380
An intentional walk?

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:51.880
Ball. Ball four!

00:15:52.800 --> 00:15:54.340
He's making fools of us!

00:15:55.150 --> 00:15:56.410
Oh, man.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:58.600
If there aren't any double plays, I'm up next.

00:15:58.600 --> 00:15:59.850
Play!

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.240
You're not getting on base.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:09.970
The fans in Chicago came out to welcome me and cheer me on.

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:12.570
I can't disappoint them any longer.

00:16:13.040 --> 00:16:17.660
Today, I came here to win!

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.190
Out!

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:22.920
All right.

00:16:22.920 --> 00:16:23.620
Damn it!

00:16:23.980 --> 00:16:29.530
Now hitting, number 56: Goro Shigeno!

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:34.890
With a great chance for the Hornets to score another run, Shigeno, the pitcher, is up at bat.

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.840
It's finally Shigeno.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:37.690
Play!

00:16:39.840 --> 00:16:43.980
I never thought I'd end up batting against you.

00:16:44.350 --> 00:16:49.690
I hate to say this, but seeing your pitches today, I can tell you're already finished.

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.150
Strike!

00:16:53.640 --> 00:16:57.410
You called me a weakling, but look at your pitch.

00:16:57.410 --> 00:17:01.560
Man, nobody wants to see you come back like this!

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:06.500
That was close.

00:17:10.900 --> 00:17:12.020
Bastard.

00:17:12.600 --> 00:17:15.340
That probably wasn't intentional, considering the bases are loaded,

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.700
but you're really going all out.

00:17:19.740 --> 00:17:20.790
Strike!

00:17:26.630 --> 00:17:27.020
Ball.

00:17:28.350 --> 00:17:29.200
All right!

00:17:29.200 --> 00:17:30.070
Good decision.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:35.400
Maybe this is fate.

00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:38.240
If you can't even get a pitcher out,

00:17:38.240 --> 00:17:40.700
I'm sure you'll be able to go back to retirement.

00:17:40.700 --> 00:17:46.710
As Honda Jr, I'll cut all your ties to baseball and end your career.

00:18:04.670 --> 00:18:05.990
It's in!

00:18:05.990 --> 00:18:06.620
Amazing!

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:10.630
The pitcher, Shigeno, hits a grand slam right to the scoreboard!

00:18:10.630 --> 00:18:12.020
Gibson gives up a hit.

00:18:12.020 --> 00:18:14.600
H-He really did it.

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:16.570
A-Are you serious?

00:18:31.960 --> 00:18:34.750
Johnson, the manager, comes out to the mound right away.

00:18:35.360 --> 00:18:37.220
He's switching pitchers.

00:18:37.220 --> 00:18:38.170
Who would have guessed?

00:18:38.170 --> 00:18:41.600
Joe Gibson gets knocked out in the first inning after giving up seven runs!

00:18:42.220 --> 00:18:44.800
Why did you even come back?

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:47.060
Get out of the major leagues!

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:01.910
What do you think of Joe Gibson's performance today, Mr. Johnson?

00:19:01.910 --> 00:19:05.360
Gibson was definitely not doing well today,

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:10.290
but I kept him on the mound because I thought he'd be able to pull through with his experience.

00:19:10.290 --> 00:19:14.130
In the end, that didn't really work out.

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:18.550
Given the way Mr. Gibson played, will he be resigning?

00:19:18.550 --> 00:19:22.400
I can't comment on that.

00:19:22.950 --> 00:19:27.770
If he's healthy, he'll play in the next game.

00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:30.350
Gibson gave up two runs in the first inning,

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:33.240
and he's not doing much better in the second, with two outs and the bases loaded.

00:19:33.240 --> 00:19:36.020
He's now pitching against Itao, who had a hit in the first.

00:19:36.020 --> 00:19:39.680
Now, will Gibson be able to pull through this?

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:47.330
One and two-thirds innings.

00:19:47.330 --> 00:19:49.660
Eight hits, two walks, six runs.

00:19:49.660 --> 00:19:51.690
Looking at your results today,

00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:56.590
we have to make this decision despite your past achievements.

00:19:57.630 --> 00:20:03.260
Joe Gibson, the Bisons will discharge you and file a waiver.

00:20:03.260 --> 00:20:08.680
For ten days, you will wait for teams who would like to take you in.

00:20:08.680 --> 00:20:10.050
Is that fine?

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:11.640
No, don't do that.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:14.760
I'm aware that I'm not good enough to play,

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:16.820
but instead of filing a waiver,

00:20:17.580 --> 00:20:19.820
can you treat it as voluntary retirement?

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:28.120
The day after Gibson's second straight knockout,

00:20:28.120 --> 00:20:31.550
America was filled with news of his retirement.

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:38.980
Goro and Junior, who questioned his return, calmly accepted the news...

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:44.490
and were back to fighting against their major league records.

00:20:45.300 --> 00:20:50.050
Goro continued to have mixed results as a pitcher,

00:20:50.050 --> 00:20:54.080
and concluded the first half of the season before the All-Star Game with seven wins and eight losses.

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:57.310
Not exactly the best record.

00:21:01.900 --> 00:21:04.030
Hey, Shigeno.

00:21:07.910 --> 00:21:08.780
Sorry.

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:13.300
I had to ask you to come all the way to Nashville with the All-Star Game coming up.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:14.150
No.

00:21:14.150 --> 00:21:14.960
It's fine.

00:21:15.440 --> 00:21:20.700
Unlike Keene and Watts who made the team, I've been bored out of my mind.

00:21:22.170 --> 00:21:25.790
You wouldn't get a chance to play with a 4.00 ERA.

00:21:25.790 --> 00:21:29.200
But as a rookie, you're doing all right.

00:21:30.140 --> 00:21:32.230
All right, huh?

00:21:34.350 --> 00:21:35.610
So, what was it?

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:37.480
You wanted to show me something, right?

00:21:40.210 --> 00:21:41.700
Here?

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:43.880
It's a minor league stadium.

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:44.620
Yeah.

00:21:45.130 --> 00:21:48.300
The home stadium of Nashville's AA team.

00:21:48.300 --> 00:21:50.030
AA?

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:55.430
Darn, it already started.

00:21:55.430 --> 00:21:57.130
Hey, wait a minute!

00:21:57.130 --> 00:22:02.940
Why did I have to come all the way here during my break to watch a AA game with you?

00:22:02.940 --> 00:22:04.370
Just sit down.

00:22:06.870 --> 00:22:08.390
Do you know which major league team

00:22:07.820 --> 00:22:08.760
Out!

00:22:08.390 --> 00:22:10.910
the Nashville Bulls are affiliated with?

00:22:10.910 --> 00:22:12.300
No!

00:22:12.300 --> 00:22:14.520
Do you know how many teams exist in the minors?

00:22:15.280 --> 00:22:17.270
The Chicago Bisons.

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:20.440
Bisons?!

00:22:20.440 --> 00:22:23.560
Isn't the Bisons where Gibson was playing—

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:34.080
G-Gibson?!

00:22:34.590 --> 00:22:36.550
Wh-What's he doing there?

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:59.140
usubeni hikaru sora kono hoshi wa nemuranai

00:22:53.220 --> 00:22:59.140
The sky glows a faint red, illuminated by a star that never sleeps.

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:04.480
yoake wa zutto yorisou

00:22:59.140 --> 00:23:04.480
The dawn will forever creep up on us.

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:10.740
kimi ga doko ni ite mo nani kangaeteitemo

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:10.740
No matter where you are, or what you're thinking,

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:15.540
mawaru hoshi chihyou wa hitotsu dake

00:23:10.740 --> 00:23:15.540
there's only earth. One spinning planet.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:22.130
ikuoku mo aru yume wo mitetayo

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:22.130
I had dreams, hundreds of millions of dreams.

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:28.010
tsukamu kibou mitsuketa ne

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:28.010
I finally found the hope I could hold on to.

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:33.850
ikuoku no yoru kimi to nagameta

00:23:28.010 --> 00:23:33.850
The sky you and I gazed up at for hundreds of millions of nights

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:39.270
sora mo tsunagatteiru

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:39.270
is always connected wherever we are.

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:45.730
zutto miteru dake no anohi no akogare no tame ni

00:23:39.270 --> 00:23:45.730
For the inspiration that I never lose sight of,

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:50.990
shinjite tsuzuketa omoi wo

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:54.450
I'll shape my life-long feelings into something tangible.

00:23:50.990 --> 00:23:54.450
zettai katachi ni suru

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:56.910
boku to yakusoku shita

00:23:54.450 --> 00:24:03.290
The place where you and I made the promise calls out to you.

00:23:56.910 --> 00:24:03.290
ano basho ga kimi wo yobuyo

00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:07.130
sotto

00:24:03.370 --> 00:24:07.130
It gently calls out to you.

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:15.300
Preview

00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:15.300
Preview

00:24:11.530 --> 00:24:13.800
Why is Gibson pitching in the minors?

00:24:13.800 --> 00:24:16.930
What in the world is that old man thinking?

00:24:16.930 --> 00:24:17.740
But...

00:24:17.740 --> 00:24:21.750
Now that I know he's working hard in the minors, I can't just twiddle my thumbs.

00:24:21.750 --> 00:24:24.980
Next time, on Major: Fully Back on the Mound.

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:26.980
Run toward the stage of your dreams!

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:28.930
Next Time

00:24:24.980 --> 00:24:28.930
Next Time

